  {"id":"B14","spot":14,"nums":{"t":2,"n":9},"q":"Luis counts 9 tomato seeds. There are 2 times as many bean seeds as tomato seeds. Which equation can be used to find the number of bean seeds, b?","choices":["2 × 9 = b","2 + 9 = b","2 × b = 9","9 − 2 = b"],"answer":"2 × 9 = b","slips":{"2 + 9 = b":{"tag":"Picked the wrong sign","say":"That equation adds. Times as many means using multiplication to compare. 2 × 9 = b."},"2 × b = 9":{"tag":"Put the unknown in the wrong place","say":"b is the larger number, the product: the total for the bottom bar. 9 is the smaller number, the top box. 2 × 9 = b."},"9 − 2 = b":{"tag":"Picked the wrong sign","say":"That equation subtracts. Times as many means using multiplication to compare. 2 × 9 = b."}},"explanation":"2 times as many as 9 means 2 × 9. So 2 × 9 = b. The product, b, is the total for the bottom bar.","explain":{"mult":{"top":"tomato seeds","bottom":"bean seeds","n":9,"t":2,"ask":"letter","letter":"b"}}},
  {"id":"B15","spot":15,"nums":{"t":5,"n":4},"q":"Owen has 4 kites. Sam has 5 times as many kites as Owen. Which equation can be used to find the number of kites, k, for Sam?","choices":["5 × 4 = k","5 + 4 = k","5 × k = 4","5 − 4 = k"],"answer":"5 × 4 = k","slips":{"5 + 4 = k":{"tag":"Picked the wrong sign","say":"That equation adds. Times as many means using multiplication to compare. 5 × 4 = k."},"5 × k = 4":{"tag":"Put the unknown in the wrong place","say":"k is the larger number, the product: the total for the bottom bar. 4 is the smaller number, the top box. 5 × 4 = k."},"5 − 4 = k":{"tag":"Picked the wrong sign","say":"That equation subtracts. Times as many means using multiplication to compare. 5 × 4 = k."}},"explanation":"5 times as many as 4 means 5 × 4. So 5 × 4 = k. The product, k, is the total for the bottom bar.","explain":{"mult":{"top":"Owen","bottom":"Sam","n":4,"t":5,"ask":"letter","letter":"k"}}},
  {"id":"B16","spot":16,"nums":{"t":4,"n":7},"q":"On Saturday, Ben did 28 jumping jacks. That is 4 times as many jumping jacks as on Tuesday. Part A: Which equation can be used to find how many jumping jacks, j, Ben did on Tuesday?","choices":["28 ÷ 4 = j","28 × 4 = j","28 − 4 = j","28 + 4 = j"],"answer":"28 ÷ 4 = j","slips":{"28 × 4 = j":{"tag":"Multiplied instead of dividing","say":"Tuesday had fewer jumping jacks. 28 is 4 times as many. Divide: 28 ÷ 4 = j."},"28 − 4 = j":{"tag":"Picked the wrong sign","say":"Times as many is not take away. Divide to find the smaller number: 28 ÷ 4 = j."},"28 + 4 = j":{"tag":"Picked the wrong sign","say":"Tuesday had fewer. Divide to find the smaller number: 28 ÷ 4 = j."}},"explanation":"28 jumping jacks on Saturday is 4 times as many as on Tuesday. Divide to find the smaller number: 28 ÷ 4 = j.","explain":{"mult":{"top":"Tuesday","bottom":"Saturday","n":"j","t":4,"ask":"small","total":28}}},
  {"id":"B17","spot":17,"nums":{"t":4,"n":7},"q":"On Saturday, Ben did 28 jumping jacks. That is 4 times as many jumping jacks as on Tuesday. Part B: How many jumping jacks did Ben do on Tuesday?","choices":["7","24","112","32"],"answer":"7","slips":{"24":{"tag":"Subtracted instead of dividing","say":"You subtracted 28 − 4. Divide: 28 ÷ 4 = 7."},"32":{"tag":"Added instead of dividing","say":"You added. Tuesday had fewer. Divide: 28 ÷ 4 = 7."},"112":{"tag":"Multiplied instead of dividing","say":"You multiplied. Tuesday had fewer. Divide: 28 ÷ 4 = 7."}},"explanation":"28 ÷ 4 = 7. Check: 4 × 7 = 28. Ben did 7 jumping jacks on Tuesday.","explain":{"mult":{"top":"Tuesday","bottom":"Saturday","n":7,"t":4,"ask":null}}}
